Z||000000||fropuff||03-05-2001||04:26 PM||||Yes, that is a smilie.  For those who know the car that I'm driving now, a 1980 Olds Cutlass Supreme LS; a.k.a. Ghetto Cruiser, Bessie, POS, etc., etc.  Anyway, this car is no more.  Yep, I finally blew the engine on it.  It had 90.8K on it; turned over today.  It didn't blow, but something's f'd up and I don't want to fix it; not worth the money.  Anyway, I was thinking of parting it out, but there is no demand for 1980 Oldsmobile parts.  I want to sell it to a salvage yard, and I was wondering what they would give me.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||10
Z||000001||rogergarrison||03-05-2001||04:35 PM||||there only gonna give you what the weight in scrap is $50-$75. One big yard here wanted to give me $75 for a 88 Dodge minivan, had new paint, perfect body, new shock,brakes and tires. It ran fine, but had cracked head. Needless to say they didnt get it.||||reg||1
